From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] venus: Vulkan on Windows over the viogpu3d kernel driver

Venus (Mesa's Vulkan driver for virtio-gpu) runs on Linux over the DRM
ioctls; Mesa 26 has the start of a Windows build but no renderer for it. This
adds one for the viogpu3d kernel driver (virtio-gpu's Windows driver, with
WinBoat's Venus escapes) and what the build needs:

- vn_renderer_wddm.c: finds the virtio-gpu adapter among all adapters (in an
  RDP session the desktop belongs to a remote adapter), creates a D3DKMT
  device that carries the Venus context, and uses the escapes VIOGPU_GET_CAPS
  and VIOGPU_CTX_INIT, then VIOGPU_BLOB_CREATE/MAP/DESTROY for shared memory
  and host-visible memory and VIOGPU_EXECBUFFER for command streams.
  Renderer syncs are timelines: the submissions that signal them carry an
  event the kernel driver sets once the ring's fence signals; a wait for a
  value nothing signals yet waits for the submission that will (Vulkan lets a
  fence be waited for before its submission, which Venus' present thread
  does). No external memory or syncs. The adapter's LUID goes to
  VkPhysicalDeviceIDProperties, so D3D12 on Vulkan (vkd3d-proton) finds the
  Vulkan device of a DXGI adapter, and vk_icdEnumerateAdapterPhysicalDevices
  gives the Windows loader Venus' devices by adapter (the common runtime's
  looks at a device list Venus doesn't use): the loader then sorts them by
  DXGI adapter and puts layered drivers on the same adapter after them
  (Dozen, from Microsoft's OpenCL/OpenGL/Vulkan compatibility pack, came
  first before, so programs picking the first GPU took Vulkan on D3D12).
- The escapes' structures in src/virtio/wddm/viogpu_wddm_driver.h (as the
  kernel driver's).
- VK_KHR_win32_surface is offered (the instance offered no surface at all).
- Build with clang-cl (Venus needs C11 atomics and typeof, which MSVC lacks):
  u_atomic.h uses the GCC builtins with clang-cl (its intrin.h lacks the
  lowercase _interlocked* names); the -Bsymbolic and dynamic-list checks are
  skipped for MSVC-style compilers (clang-cl passes -Wl, options to lld-link,
  which takes them for input files); vk_spec_info_to_nir_spirv moves to a file
  of its own, so a driver without a compiler doesn't link the SPIR-V to NIR
  compiler's symbols; pid_t and no-op sync-file helpers for the Windows CRT;
  the DLL exports through vulkan_api.def, and the new vulkan-virtio-dll-name
  option names it and its manifest, which sits next to it (the kernel
  driver's INF names the manifest) with a path relative to it.

Tested in a Windows 11 guest on an RTX 3080 host (WinBoat's image 6.05-9):
memory, compute, rendering, texture sampling, timeline semaphores and a
swapchain, 64- and 32-bit; D3D12 through vkd3d-proton.
